-- title:
--   Degree of the weight-2m floor divisor in characteristic 3
-- statement:
--   Let $N \ge 1$ be an integer with $3 \nmid N$ admitting a prime divisor $q$ with $q \equiv 2 \pmod 3$, let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $3$, and let $m$ be a natural number. Write $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFullC K N` for the intermediate field of the Laurent series field over $K$ generated by the $q$-expansions `qExpand K d (jqModC K)` for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$, where `jqModC K` is the reduction of the $j$-expansion $q^{-1}E_4^3\eta^{-24}$; places of $F$ over $K$ are valuation subrings containing $K$, different from $F$, whose ring is a principal ideal ring, and $\operatorname{ord}_w$ is the associated normalised integer valuation. Let $D$ be a divisor on $F$, i.e. a finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued function on these places, and suppose that for every place $w$, writing $e_w = \operatorname{ord}_w \bar j$ with $\bar j$ the class of `jqModC K` in $F$ and $e'_w = \operatorname{ord}_w(\bar j - 1728)$ (note $1728 = 0$ in $K$, so $e'_w = e_w$), one has $$D(w) = \big[e_w > 0\big]\,\Big\lfloor \tfrac{2m e_w}{3}\Big\rfloor + \big[e'_w > 0\big]\,\Big\lfloor \tfrac{m e'_w}{2}\Big\rfloor + \big[e_w < 0\big]\, m e_w,$$ the quotients being integer division. Then the degree of $D$ — the sum of its values weighted by the residue degrees of the places — satisfies, as a rational number, $$\deg D = m\,(2\,\mathrm{genusFormula}(N) - 2) + \lfloor m/2\rfloor\,\nu_2(N) + \lfloor 2m/3\rfloor\,\nu_3(N) + m\,\nu_\infty(N),$$ where $\nu_2(N)$ and $\nu_3(N)$ count the solutions in $\mathbb{Z}/N$ of $x^2+1=0$ and of $x^2+x+1=0$, $\nu_\infty(N) = \sum_{d \mid N}\varphi(\gcd(d, N/d))$, and $\mathrm{genusFormula}(N) = 1 + \psi(N)/12 - \nu_2(N)/4 - \nu_3(N)/3 - \nu_\infty(N)/2$ with $\psi(N) = \sum_{d \mid N,\ d \text{ squarefree}} N/d$; the floors $\lfloor m/2\rfloor$ and $\lfloor 2m/3\rfloor$ are natural-number divisions.
--
--   This is the characteristic-$3$ counterpart of the computation of the degree of the divisor of weight-$2m$ floor type on the modular curve $X_0(N)$, whose right-hand side is the familiar expression $m(2g-2) + \lfloor m/2\rfloor\nu_2 + \lfloor 2m/3\rfloor\nu_3 + m\nu_\infty$ in the genus numerics of $X_0(N)$; in characteristic $3$ the two elliptic branches both see the places above $\bar j = 0$, where the ramification index is $3$ or $6$ under the hypotheses on $N$. It feeds the Riemann–Roch dimension bound [`ModularCurve.card_le_dimFormula_of_isModPFormFn_of_linearIndependent_of_charP_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.card_le_dimFormula_of_isModPFormFn_of_linearIndependent_of_charP_three) for spaces of mod $3$ modular forms.
